      en: "Tanjong Maya is a village in Tutong District, famous for traditional wooden boat building. Located on the Tutong River, craftsmen construct fishing boats using age-old techniques. The economy revolves around boatbuilding, fishing, and agriculture. The village has a mosque, a primary school, and a community hall. Residents take pride in their maritime heritage. An annual boat festival features races and exhibitions. The river provides abundant fish, supporting local livelihoods. Tanjong Maya is also known for its grilled fish dishes and traditional cakes.",
